# Text files are stored with LF in the repository and checked out in the
# platform's own convention, regardless of anyone's core.autocrlf setting.
* text=auto

# iCalendar requires CRLF (RFC 5545 3.1) and feed/latest.ics is served straight
# out of the repository by raw.githubusercontent.com, so its bytes must survive
# unchanged. Normalising it to LF produces a file strict calendar clients reject.
*.ics -text
